UID:10211-1792933200-1792942200@thespaceforart.com
SUMMARY:Marking Movement: A Journey Through 5Rhythms and Intuitive Painting
DESCRIPTION:Marking Movement: A Journey Through 5Rhythms and Intuitive Painting\nSayrah Garrison and Naz Botas | October 25 | 1 – 3:30 pm | The Space | $55 — 12 spots available \nThe Space invites you to give expression to your movements through intuitive painting.  This is not creation from the level of thought\, but rather from your inner intuition and guidance. \nMarking Movement brings together two powerful languages of self-expression – 5Rhythms movement meditation and intuitive painting – into one continuous\, embodied experience. \nThe 5Rhythms Practice\nCreated by Gabrielle Roth\, 5Rhythms is a conscious dance practice rooted in the principle that when we put the psyche in motion\, it can begin to heal itself. The five rhythms – Flowing\, Staccato\, Chaos\, Lyrical\, and Stillness – each offer a different quality of movement and energy\, helping us cultivate grounded bodies\, clear minds\, and inspired spirits. \nGuided by the 5Rhythms map\, we’ll take a deep dive into our own inner landscape\, moving beyond choreography and expectations to reconnect with our authentic selves. As we become more present in our bodies\, we create space to listen more deeply to what is moving through us\, including the art that wants to emerge. \nFrom Movement to Mark-Making\nWe’ll move through the session in cycles: approximately ten minutes of dance followed by ten minutes of painting\, repeating as we travel through the five rhythms. Rather than stopping to think about what to paint\, you’ll carry the energy and sensation of each rhythm directly from the dance floor to the wall\, allowing your hands to express what your body has just discovered. \nAnd there’s a twist: none of the paintings belong to just one person. \nAll twelve stations – each one ready with its own large sheet of paper taped to the wall\, along with colored chalk pastels\, charcoal\, tempera paint\, brushes\, and pencils – are shared by the whole group. Throughout the class\, everyone moves from station to station\, adding their mark to artwork others have already begun. \nBy the end\, twelve collaborative paintings will emerge\, each one holding traces of the collective movement\, energy\, intuition\, and presence of the entire group. There is no need to finish “your” piece and no ownership to protect. Instead\, the paintings become a visual conversation\, like the way we dance with one another.  One person’s Chaos layered over another’s Flowing\, one moment of Stillness resting beside someone else’s Lyrical expression – it will all result in works of beauty. \nThis is an opportunity to bring our deepest prayers to life through conscious movement and intuitive art\, while experiencing the creative energy that emerges when we move and make in community. \nNo dance experience or art experience is required.  Just bring a willingness to move without choreography and paint without a plan. Come ready to get out of your head\, into your body\, and onto the wall. \nWhat to Expect\nFive rounds of 5Rhythms-inspired movement\, each followed by ten minutes of free\, intuitive painting at a shared station. All art supplies are provided. \nWear comfortable clothing that allows you to move freely and that you don’t mind getting a little paint on. \nSpace is limited to 12 participants to keep the experience intimate and the twelve shared paintings feeling personal and alive. \nMeet Your Facilitator\nSayrah Garrison is an accredited 5Rhythms teacher who lives and works in Northern New Jersey. She has been dancing the 5Rhythms since 2001 and teaching since 2014. A social worker and mother\, Sayrah is passionate about the healing arts and the transformative potential of movement\, creativity\, and community. \nJoin us for this unique wellness experience — a space to move\, listen\, create\, and discover what wants to flow through you.
